cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "REACHOUT's planned nature-based solutions and building-level pluvial flood risk in Logroño"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
- family-names: "Fouilloux"
  given-names: "Anne"
  orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1784-2920"
  affiliation: "LifeWatch ERIC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/annefou/logrono-planned-nbs-flood-risk"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
abstract: >-
  Do the nature-based solutions of REACHOUT's planned scenario for Logroño (Spain) reduce building-level
  pluvial flood risk? Using the result tables of the Logroño flood-adaptation scenarios analysis (v0.1.0) and the
  REACHOUT flood maps, this repository compares both versions of the planned scenario (with and without extra ponds)
  with the current green cover under present and future design rainfall, for return periods of 2 to 200 years.
  It holds one FORRT nanopublication chain (question-rooted) and its headline figure.
# Identifiers below are recorded AUTOMATICALLY on each release by
# .github/workflows/release-identifiers.yml — don't fill them in by hand.
#
# `doi:` is the CONCEPT DOI: it means "cite this project" and deliberately
# resolves to whatever version is latest. That floating behaviour is correct
# HERE and wrong in a nanopub — see scripts/set_release_identifiers.py.
#
# (This used to say "run /init-template again or edit by hand". /init-template
# deletes itself as its final step, so by the time a DOI existed the skill it
# named was gone and "edit by hand" was the only path left. Two repos built from
# this template then recorded the version DOI two different ways — one a
# structured identifier, one a prose comment. Hence the automation.)
